{
  "spec": "0.3",
  "_comment": [
    "The query corpus: questions that can only be answered by comparing a batch of paths together.",
    "The color of a single path is what `eval.json` covers, whereas here the questions are about block roots, the exceptions that cut through a block root, counts,",
    "the nodes a document declares that are absent from the real tree, and the reason why.",
    "Paths are always segment arrays. The values of via are in docs/*/contract.md:",
    "  subtree  = tinted directly by `@`",
    "  explicit = tinted directly by `>`",
    "  inherited = propagated down from an ancestor, which does not count as an operation"
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "queries/roots-of",
      "note": "When the whole mods subtree is delete, the block root reported is mods alone rather than every layer beneath it",
      "source": "- mods\n    @ delete\n    > protect\n        | player-save.dat\n        - textures\n- obsolete\n    @ delete\n",
      "paths": [
        [
          "mods"
        ],
        [
          "mods",
          "cache"
        ],
        [
          "mods",
          "player-save.dat"
        ],
        [
          "mods",
          "textures"
        ],
        [
          "mods",
          "textures",
          "custom.png"
        ],
        [
          "obsolete"
        ],
        [
          "obsolete",
          "old"
        ]
      ],
      "roots_of": {
        "delete": [
          [
            "mods"
          ],
          [
            "obsolete"
          ]
        ]
      },
      "counts": {
        "delete": 4,
        "protect": 3
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "queries/exceptions-within",
      "note": "Which rules cut through a block root, which is the raw material for the predicate asking whether a removed root's scope contains protect",
      "source": "- mods\n    @ delete\n    > protect\n        | player-save.dat\n        - textures\n",
      "paths": [
        [
          "mods"
        ],
        [
          "mods",
          "cache"
        ],
        [
          "mods",
          "player-save.dat"
        ],
        [
          "mods",
          "textures"
        ],
        [
          "mods",
          "textures",
          "custom.png"
        ]
      ],
      "exceptions_within": [
        {
          "root": [
            "mods"
          ],
          "paths": [
            [
              "mods",
              "player-save.dat"
            ],
            [
              "mods",
              "textures"
            ],
            [
              "mods",
              "textures",
              "custom.png"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "queries/paths-with-and-counts",
      "source": "- root\n    @ default\n    > special\n        | fileA\n",
      "paths": [
        [
          "root"
        ],
        [
          "root",
          "fileA"
        ],
        [
          "root",
          "fileB"
        ]
      ],
      "paths_with": {
        "special": [
          [
            "root",
            "fileA"
          ]
        ]
      },
      "counts": {
        "default": 2,
        "special": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "queries/unmatched-declarations",
      "note": "Under the open world a node declared but absent from the real tree is entirely normal, yet the caller wants to know which ones there are.",
      "source": "- root\n    @ default\n    - nowhere\n        @ special\n",
      "paths": [
        [
          "root",
          "a"
        ]
      ],
      "eval": [
        {
          "path": [
            "root",
            "a"
          ],
          "color": "default"
        },
        {
          "path": [
            "root",
            "nowhere"
          ],
          "color": "special"
        }
      ],
      "unmatched": [
        [
          "root",
          "nowhere"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "queries/unmatched-accepts-a-covered-declaration",
      "note": "Only the leaf path is given, and the intermediate directory does not count as unmatched, since otherwise a caller that supplies only leaves would be flooded with false reports",
      "source": "- root\n    @ default\n    - mid\n        @ special\n",
      "paths": [
        [
          "root",
          "mid",
          "leaf"
        ]
      ],
      "unmatched": []
    },
    {
      "name": "queries/explain-chain",
      "note": "The whole covering chain in ascending line order, where the last entry takes effect",
      "source": "- mods\n    @ delete\n    > protect\n        - saves\n",
      "paths": [
        [
          "mods",
          "saves"
        ]
      ],
      "explain": [
        {
          "path": [
            "mods",
            "saves"
          ],
          "chain": [
            {
              "color": "delete",
              "line": 2,
              "via": "inherited"
            },
            {
              "color": "protect",
              "line": 3,
              "via": "explicit"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "queries/explain-source-lines",
      "note": "The source line: this verdict comes from line 3",
      "source": "- root\n    @ default\n    > special\n        | fileA\n",
      "paths": [
        [
          "root",
          "fileA"
        ]
      ],
      "explain": [
        {
          "path": [
            "root",
            "fileA"
          ],
          "chain": [
            {
              "color": "default",
              "line": 2,
              "via": "inherited"
            },
            {
              "color": "special",
              "line": 3,
              "via": "explicit"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "queries/explain-marks-inherited",
      "note": "A color that was inherited is marked inherited, since it should not count as an operation in a preview",
      "source": "- root\n    @ default\n",
      "paths": [
        [
          "root",
          "deep",
          "down"
        ]
      ],
      "explain": [
        {
          "path": [
            "root",
            "deep",
            "down"
          ],
          "chain": [
            {
              "color": "default",
              "line": 2,
              "via": "inherited"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "queries/explain-none-when-nothing-reaches",
      "source": "- root\n    @ default\n",
      "paths": [
        [
          "elsewhere"
        ]
      ],
      "eval": [
        {
          "path": [
            "elsewhere"
          ],
          "color": null
        }
      ],
      "explain": [
        {
          "path": [
            "elsewhere"
          ],
          "chain": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "queries/source-columns-survive-bom-and-crlf",
      "note": "A column number is 1-based and equals indentation plus 1, pointing at the symbol of the declaration. This source carries a BOM, CRLF and non-ASCII at once, which incidentally shows that parsing is unaffected by all three. Only ASCII spaces can precede a symbol, so counting scalars and counting bytes agree in this case, and what it pins down is the 1-based start and the indentation. See rust/docs/*/api.md.",
      "source": "﻿- 中文名\r\n    @ 红色\r\n",
      "paths": [
        [
          "中文名"
        ]
      ],
      "explain": [
        {
          "path": [
            "中文名"
          ],
          "chain": [
            {
              "color": "红色",
              "line": 2,
              "col": 5,
              "via": "subtree"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
